> Currently i
> am learning a lot of things from trying the protection run. 

Like how to die?

Neutral humans aren't exactly made for the protection racket, since
_none_ of the common mine inhabitants will be peaceful towards them.
Gnomes and dwarfs are good for the purpose, and lawful humans will at
least get mostly peaceful dwarfs.

> Here is my
> situation:
> 
>   |-----.|
> --|.[[@h.|
> ....h..--
> .....f.|
> .......|
> .......|
> Molnar, the neutral human monk - 
> Dlvl 3, HP 8(14) Pw 4(4) AC 4 XL:1/2, Hungry

Since the dwarf has just now moved into range, you're not in immediate
danger. Unless they've hasted themselves by potion or wand, dwarfs
move at half normal speed. You could step south (to the grid adjacent
sw to the dwarf to your right) without being hit, and then try to keep
your pet between you and them.

> Significant inventory
> a - an uncursed +2 pair of leather gloves (beeing worn)
> b - an uncursed +1 robe
> f - 2 uncursed potions of healing
> g - a blessed potion of healing

Down the two uncursed potions as soon as you have a few turns out of
immediate danger. Two additional max hitpoints will give you a bit
more maneuvring space.

I hope you're actually _wearing_ that robe. Unfortunately, at a mere 4
pp max, you won't be able to use your starting spell before you level
up.

> A black potion has been
> thrown at me and hit the dwarf to the left ~10 turns ago without effect
> ("the potion evaporates").

You should have been offered the opportunity to call the black potion
something - potions thrown at you are generally something which will
be harmful when hit by them or quaffing them; even if you don't know
what exactly the effect is, you could at least call the potion 'black,
harmful' to make sure you don't accidentally quaff one.

> Last turn, Shakira finished eating a corpse and missed the dwarf to my
> left.

Incidentally, pets can get killed in the mines - there are so many
foes there that a pet's life regeneration often can't cope. The
chances of 'pacifistically' getting to minetown without a pet and
against a hostile mines population are rather slim.

[options]
> * stepping south, giving the dwarf to my right a chance to hit (and
> kill?) me. I have also seen the other dwarf picking up a crossbow last
> turn, so he would have a chance to fire at me as well.

In order to shoot, the dwarf needs to have some crossbow bolts, too.
If he hasn't picked up some of those, there's no danger of that. 

> What would you do in this situation? Is it possible to live without
> killing a dwarf? Will a single hit from a dwarf kill me?

Depends on what the dwarf is wielding. If it's nothing or a dagger,
that's impossible to unlikely at eight current hitpoints. If it's a
pick-axe or a sword, it's a definite possibility. If it's a mattock
('heavy pick', i think), it's quite likely.

> One last thing: I am playing without engraving the e-word. Dusting it
> is NOT an option.

Is it commented out of the source?

If not, it is an option you won't like, but an option nevertheless. 

